>>
Rule 1 (input must be a tensor argument)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (input dtype must be real; complex dtypes not supported)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 3 (when out is provided, its shape must match the input exactly)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 5 (when out is provided, input and out dtypes should match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
